WEBVTT

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.020
A farmer's day starts early.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.290
Then you heroes will also...

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:07.420
Yes, we'll be participating as mercenaries.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.070
That's very reassuring.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.400
I am Cantil.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.370
I have fought in many battles against orcs.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:15.910
I'm Yotsuya—

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.160
Hey, nice to know ya, Cantil-san!

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.570
Man, that's so cool!

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:23.340
I'm so glad we have a guy on 
our side who's been there!

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:28.660
Excellent.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.070
Hell yeah!

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:35.240
An orc's weapons are the massive 
fists unleashed by their long arms.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.000
A direct hit from one means instant death.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.440
For that reason, you must attack 
efficiently and withdraw immediately.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.070
The key to fighting orcs is to stay 
outside their range at all times.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.640
<i>So it's what they call "hit and run tactics."</i>

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.340
Okay!

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.030
You.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.470
With short blades like those, 
you're likely to take a fatal wound.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.620
Do you have another weapon?

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.360
Uh, no. These are all I have.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.490
Don't worry, Yotsuya.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.820
We Warriors will take care 
of those orcs for ya.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.210
Right, Iu-chan?

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.120
<b>Pass</b>

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.830
<b>Didn't Make the Team</b>

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.110
I thought anyone who couldn't 
wield a sword could use a bow,

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.260
but if you can't do that, either...

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.700
Sorry.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.510
Uh, yeah, I'm not <i>that</i> eager 
to get in on this fight.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.910
I'll go raise my level!

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.920
<i>Damn it! I didn't make the team?</i>

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.310
<i>Just wait!</i>

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.740
<i>I'll be back before you know it!</i>

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.310
Monsters other than orcs?

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.700
Ain't nothin' like that on this island.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.310
What?

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:43.460
Our ancestors killed 'em 
all off ages ago. Right?

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.490
Yeah. Our island's proud of that.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.410
<i>Experience is normally gained 
by defeating monsters.</i>

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.410
<i>Other ways to get it include using 
magic, if you're a Wizard...</i>

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.540
<i>or cooking, if you're a Chef.</i>

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.670
<i>It can be gained by performing 
tasks that are part of your job.</i>

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.530
<i>Which means...</i>

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.460
I want to farm!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.380
Yer pretty good at that.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.220
Yeah, my grandparents were farmers.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.140
I helped them a lot when I was little.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.330
That's admirable!

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:22.930
Wait, this ain't why we 
asked you to come here!

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:26.760
An earthquake?

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.400
Pretty big one, too...

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.610
What's going on?!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.690
Damn, those are damaged now.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.250
It happens all the time.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:44.140
The fruits on this island 
don't grow too big.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.460
A quake like that'll always 
knock 'em right down.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.390
It's 'cause there ain't enough 
nutrients in the soil.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.010
Nutrients...

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.800
What fertilizer do you use?

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.800
We've always used Buffo dung,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.950
but since there are less 
Buffo around these days,

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.480
there ain't enough of that, either.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.100
<i>Feeding the orcs is having an effect 
on island agriculture, too?</i>

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.090
<i>Jiffon is a volcanic island.</i>

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:12.420
<i>Since its surface is 
covered in volcanic soil,</i>

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.710
<i>it lacks the organic matter 
that nourishes plants.</i>

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.840
<i>If there's a fertilizer we can 
substitute for Buffo dung...</i>

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.390
Seaweed and shells?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.040
You can really use these as fertilizer?

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.730
First, you mix seaweed 
with the soil like this,

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.420
then you wait for it to break down.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.790
So we can't just spread it 
on the fields as it is?

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.060
It doesn't work raw.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.970
Mold grows on it, which causes 
even more crop death.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.900
Huh...

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.100
If we mix Buffo dung into it later, 
the microbes will hasten the—

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.740
Hey! Where are you lookin'?!

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.190
Yana is... no!

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:51.230
Yana's boobs are mine!

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.170
Stop!

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:52.980
I won't let anyone else have 'em!

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.070
Th-There's a man watching!

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:58.300
<i>Does that mean they do this regularly 
when no men are watching?!</i>

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:01.730
You two sure are close. 
You're always together.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:05.430
I keep an eye on Yana to make 
sure no nasty pests get to her!

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.640
Uh, really, I'm not...

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.930
Gah! He ain't the slightest 
bit interested in me!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.330
You've got some nerve, shootin' 
Yana down like that!

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.550
<i>What do you want from me?</i>

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.080
Anyway, to be serious about it,

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.410
we Väikedaam have to remain virgins.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.590
If we lose our virginity, 
we have to quit the role.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.980
But there's no one to take 
our place right now.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.530
Virgins...

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.840
Um... And you two are how old?

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:36.930
When I took over as Väikedaam at age 
12, I thought I'd marry at 18 or so

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:43.920
<b>25 Years Old</b>

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:43.920
<b>25 Years Old</b>

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:43.920
<b>27 Years Old</b>

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:43.920
<b>27 Years Old</b>

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.960
and be able to quit the job...

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.580
We missed our chance to marry entirely!

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.630
We can't even keep up with the 
stuff people our age are into!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.810
<i>That hurt them worse than I expected!</i>

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.450
And it's all 'cause there are no 
girls here to take our place!

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:55.320
Hang in there, Yana! I'm sure 
in just a few more years...

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.870
Wait, is it because of the orcs 
that you have no successors?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:06:59.720
Yep.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:04.640
All the girls who were s'posed 
to become Väikedaam got eaten.

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:10.460
<i>At any rate, I have to level 
up, whatever it takes!</i>

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.490
Roasted beans, fried rice-style, 
wish shellfish and root vegetables.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.400
<i>First, I'll cook the shellfish 
I got from the sea</i>

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.340
Looks tasty!

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.870
<i>to gain experience as a Chef.</i>

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.880
Sure does!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.320
<i>Then I'll crush the leftover shells,</i>

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.480
<i>add Buffo dung, and...</i>

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.370
All right. That's a healthy-smelling stench.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.750
<i>There are hot springs all over 
the volcanic island of Jiffon.</i>

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:36.460
<i>Its hot, humid environment is 
perfect for microbe reproduction.</i>

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.300
Creature magic!

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.810
I'll speed up the reproduction and 
decomposing behavior of these microbes!

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.070
Wow, I don't believe it!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:52.910
I had no idea you could make 
fertilizer so quickly.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.460
Actually, it usually takes more time,

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.440
but this is a special occasion.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.630
I needed it to level up.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.870
This is a lot of menial labor...

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:08.680
Hey, do you have a radio or anything?

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:09.720
Radio?

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:13.890
I'd like some music or something 
to take my mind off the work.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:17.570
Oh, well, that's our job!

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.170
There's a ritual song that's 
been handed down here for ages!

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:22.440
Aoiu, let's get ready right now!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.160
Yeah!

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.420
A ritual song?

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.610
Like the folk songs farmers 
sing when working in fields?

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.070
Huh?

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.570
Now, as the 100th generation 
of Väikedaam...

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:46.960
We will perform the legendary hit 
number of the past 800 years.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.080
Please listen.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.890
"The Song of the Many Islands."

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:56.080
<i>Hear our song of rituals and miso</i>

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.630
<i>Dumplings of music from the eastern isle</i>

00:08:58.630 --> 00:08:59.960
<i>The earth shakes</i>

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:01.340
<i>My feelings burst</i>

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.100
<i>Plow the fields, heave-ho!</i>

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.150
<i>Tofu and jelly noodles on a withered shore</i>

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:19.400
<i>The mountain god blasts down 
the pillars in his fury</i>

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:25.100
<i>The sea god will devour 
you along with the shore</i>

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.420
Yana!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.830
<i>The blood of the earth pours down like rain</i>

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.760
Aoiu!

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.640
What is gonna...

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.500
...happen to us?

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.500
<i>Hear our song of rituals and miso</i>

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:40.150
<i>Dumplings of music from the eastern isle</i>

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.600
<i>On this island inhabited by the gods</i>

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.450
<i>We offer this song to you</i>

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.860
What the hell?! That was an idol song!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.950
m 0 0 l 260 0 l 260 160 l 0 160

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.950
[Experience Points]

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.950
• Gaining experience points raises the player's 
\h\hjob rank. At rank 10, the player changes jobs.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.000
You—

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:19.900
Whoa...

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.060
Too slow.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:26.020
Ryce-san! What is with your reflexes?!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.430
Here you go.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.860
Keep up the good work.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:29.750
Thank you.

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.550
Here you go.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:32.760
Thanks.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.630
And you, too.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.790
The nurturing type of girl...

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.290
Are you ditching training, too, Katz-san?

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.730
No, I'm not.

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:50.830
I'm making a map of the island.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:51.620
A map?

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:56.560
Understanding the lay of the land is an 
important part of preparing for battle.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.230
Of course, half of this is 
just because it's my hobby.

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:01.000
I'm done with this!

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:05.790
If you can't handle this level of training,

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.630
you'll never defeat the orcs.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:10.260
That's what we called you guys here for!

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.490
We're payin' y'all a lot of money!

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:14.990
The mercenaries should be 
the only ones fightin'!

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:15.890
What?

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.830
Relax, Lolle.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.310
He does have a point.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:26.680
But listen to me. This isn't about 
money. It's about determination.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.820
Either we eradicate all of the orcs,

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:33.060
or we fail and all of us die. 
Those are our options.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.500
That's what it means to attack orcs.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.440
W-Well, I was against this 
from the start, anyway!

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.010
It's insanity!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.670
Yer just bringin' this up now?!

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:45.150
We all agreed that we had 
to take out the orcs!

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:48.350
But if it's gonna end with all 
of us dead when we screw it up,

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:51.640
we're better off givin' 'em our 
Buffo like we always have!

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.260
What?! Our blood, sweat, and tears 
go into raisin' those Buffo!

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:56.410
These guys are getting on my nerves.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.950
You can't blame them. 
Their lives depend on this.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.550
They can't revive like we can.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.150
Why didn't y'all bring more 
of yer buddies with ya?!

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.780
You've got money! 
You discriminatin' against us?!

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.510
Oh, come, now. Of course not.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.460
Mercenaries value their 
lives over money, too.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:13.300
It's actually a miracle 
that you managed to get

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:18.000
five of us who are crazy enough to 
fight a war we'll probably lose.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.420
I don't care if it's a miracle! Just win!

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.420
Hey, look!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:23.720
It's an orc!

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.950
I'll go!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.180
You're fast.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.640
I can see how you escaped as the only 
surviving remnant of your people!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.060
<i>The only survivor?</i>

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:33.990
You won't get past me!

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.520
Nice, Iu-chan!

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.920
<b>Dead</b>

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.920
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.920
<b>Torii Keita</b>

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.920
<b>Dead</b>

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.920
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.920
<b>Shindou Iu</b>

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.790
I knew he was on another level,

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.710
but it's clear he has 
experience fighting orcs.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:05.420
That's going to cost a 
ton of time and stamina.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:06.330
But...

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.000
It's working!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:10.860
Outta the way!

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.870
He cut them?!

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.320
But that thing's fingers 
are like hunks of iron!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.570
<b>Dead</b>

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.570
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.490
<b>Shindou Iu</b>

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:30.490
<b>Revived</b>

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.920
<i>This is how a battle with an orc goes?</i>

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.760
<i>And there are 14 more of these guys?</i>

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:45.910
Why'd an orc come down from 
the castle today of all days?

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:48.380
Ya think they got wind of our plan?!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.170
There's a traitor!

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:56.820
There's a traitor on the island who's 
been tellin' the orcs our plans!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.380
Stop it!

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.500
The whole island's gotta come 
together to fight right now!

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.040
What're you talkin' about?

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:11.040
You two are the ones who went 
an' called mercenaries here.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:13.880
Yeah! We were against it!

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.270
Our island was peaceful before!

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:18.800
We're divided now 'cause of you two!

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:21.210
That's mean...

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.680
Fully grown men shouldn't be 
blaming women for their problems!

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:26.220
Gross!

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:30.560
Well, shit. I wanna punch these 
guys more than the orcs.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.380
All of you, stop screwing around!

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.040
Thanza?

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.490
Aren't you Thanzamer, the kid who ran away?

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.010
You finally remember me, huh?

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:47.680
That's right. I come from this island.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.960
And that's why I'm about to say this...

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:55.170
What would our ancestors think 
if they saw us right now?

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:02.040
It was 900 years ago

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:07.960
when our ancestors came to this island 
in search of peace and freedom.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:11.990
Ya don't <i>find</i> paradise. Ya make it yerself.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:16.120
This island was an uninhabited wasteland, 
but our ancestors cultivated it.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:20.220
Over years and years, they made 
it the Jiffon Island we have now.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.280
Then a little money comes into 
the equation, and this happens?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.430
Since when are you people important 
enough to buy life and death?

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:30.630
What is it you guys want to protect?

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:33.750
Is it money? Status?

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.520
Or your pride in a paradise you 
built with your own hands?

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:42.660
Land, people, culture, knowledge...

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.160
and our pride as the 
people of Jiffon Island.

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:48.800
Without all five of those, 
this island is just

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.090
a papier-mâché paradise!

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.010
I'm going to fight!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:58.940
I won't let this island become 
a papier-mâché paradise!

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:02.060
I'm fightin'!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.750
Yeah! This is our island!

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:05.850
Yeah!

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:07.810
The tide has turned.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:10.390
Yes. Let's win this, General.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.000
You...

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:18.990
Yes, he fought so bravely.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:22.910
I will not stand for this! I refuse!

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:26.340
I swear I will avenge him!

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.590
Congratula.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:40.230
You have reached rank 10 in 
your Wizard (Creature) occupa.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.140
Yes! Finally!

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:44.500
Blacksmith.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.900
<b>Fisherman</b>

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.900
<b>Blacksmith</b>

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.900
<b>Chef</b>

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.560
Wait, what?!

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.470
Another of the 0.5% chance ones?!

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:51.500
That's the third time! 
You're doing this on purpose!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.480
What even is the point of the roulette?!

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:54.480
Now, fare.

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:55.590
Hey, wait!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.490
A blacksmith, huh?

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:04.410
Oh, come to think of it...

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.850
There's an island called Jiffon.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:09.630
It's famous for its export 
of artisan weapons.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.080
I guess I'll take a look at my skills.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.430
<b>Rank          1</b>

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:16.070
"Can make weapons and armor."

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.350
"There are certain conditions,

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.310
but all players can use them"?

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.240
<i>Given the circumstances, this is actually...</i>

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.090
<i>just the job I needed!</i>

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:30.100
Gramps, this is the hero who 
wants to be yer apprentice.

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:33.520
Please teach me how to make 
weapons that can kill orcs!

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:45.630
It ain't likely yer gonna master 
forging in such a short time.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:48.530
Let's try makin' stuff with molds.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:52.140
Even someone who's still learnin' 
the technique can manage that.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:53.460
Got it, Master!

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:14.370
It's done!

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.080
Ta-da!

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.070
A stake that can take out an orc!

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.950
I call it the Storc!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.470
An axe with a stake on it?

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.800
And the name's a pun?

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.440
It's an unusual shape.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.120
Looks kinda... dumb.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.090
Watch what it can do 
before you call it dumb!

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:37.410
Yes!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.390
I made the Storc with a mold,

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:47.070
so I can make as many as we 
need in the time we have.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:51.940
And since Hakozaki-san and Tokitate-san 
aren't the best at close combat,

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.640
I have different weapons for them.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:54.830
Huh?!

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:56.980
Thanks, Yotsuya-kun!

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:58.820
Thanks, Yotsuya-kun.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:02.020
Well, the survival of our 
whole team depends on this.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.480
Anyway, I need to get back to work.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:08.160
So which one's your pick?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:08.660
Huh?

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.590
Out of those three.

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:15.010
Just so you know, I get Iu.

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:18.050
I put all kinds of moves on 
her while you were away,

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.350
so she's basically mine already.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:22.520
Sorry, Yuusuke!

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.680
<i>Yeah, he's definitely an idiot.</i>

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.140
<i>And since when are we on a first-name basis?</i>

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:31.060
That's the ammo for this weapon?

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.120
Yeah.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:35.480
Players normally can't use weapons 
that aren't their own gear.

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:38.790
We're lucky I have Blacksmith skills.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.410
Um, Aoiu-san was saying...

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:44.950
that you've been working every 
day with almost no sleep.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.850
That's no big deal.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:49.090
It's to keep everyone alive.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:52.370
You always say that, Yotsuya-kun...

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:54.830
It's a matter of priorities.

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:55.310
Huh?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.960
The value of life.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:00.370
Who would be more valuable to Earth alive?

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:04.380
That's what I base my decisions on.

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.730
There, it's done.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:11.020
I'll make sure you and Shindou-san 
come back alive, no matter what.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:14.890
Frankly, if Torii-san and Tokitate-san 
die, they can be replaced.

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:15.810
Huh?

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.800
Eugenics, eh? That's dangerous.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.910
It's not because of how they were born.

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:24.120
I'm basing it on the current situation 
and their future potential.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:29.460
Yes, but do those things not depend upon 
the environment they were born into?

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.360
I won't deny that.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:33.750
But if two people share the same faults,

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.890
I rank the more powerful person 
below the ordinary person.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.400
If the guy at the top is shit, 
it affects a lot more people, right?

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:42.300
Yotsuya-kun!

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.050
I have to give you that one.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.900
I find those words particularly painful.

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:53.130
I was once an officer.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:57.810
I led my army into seven battles, 
and lost all seven of them.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:59.490
My country then fell.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:02.640
You were... a general, right?

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.490
I heard Ryce-san say that

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.820
no matter who was in command, 
they still would've lost that battle.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:12.260
And that you were an excellent general.

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:15.690
No, I was a fool as a commander.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:18.330
I didn't withdraw when I should have,

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.420
and many men died as a result.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:25.840
That's why I cannot lose this 
battle, no matter what.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:27.890
<b>Stronghold</b>

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:28.560
We've done all the preparation we could.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.060
<b>High Ground</b>

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:31.260
I can't say our forces are optimal,

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:34.650
but if we can strike first and take 
the wind out of the orcs' sails...

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:33.100
<b>Hidden Weapons</b>

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.140
<b>Harbor</b>

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.660
We might have a chance.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:40.690
W-W-We've got trouble!

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:42.710
Th-The harbor...

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.140
is under attack by the orcs!

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:54.960
<b>Yana & Aoiu
Are the Väikedaam</b>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.430
Next week on <i>Million Lives</i>...

